# What Vercel should not upload.
#
# This is the SECOND layer, not the fix. The fix for the 19.36 GB storage incident is in
# src/content/covers.ts: its only `fs` call is now statically scoped to public/assets/covers, so
# Next.js's file tracer stops at that directory instead of trailing the whole repository into every
# server bundle (measured: 1189 → 316 traced entries for one route, docs/ 520 → 0).
#
# These patterns bound the upload size of the repository itself. They are deliberately limited to
# things `next build` provably never reads — see the comment on each group.

# Internal documentation, design history and review screenshots: 38 MB, read by humans, never by code.
docs/

# Local screenshot output from scripts/visual-check.mjs. Gitignored too.
artifacts/

# Test suites. `npm run build` runs `next build`, which does not import tests.
tests/

# Coverage and local browser caches.
coverage/
.playwright-cli/
.review/

# Markdown at the root is project paperwork. Keep the one file Vercel's UI can usefully show.
*.md
!README.md

# Build cache belongs to the build machine, not the upload.
.next/cache/

# NOT excluded, on purpose:
#   src/      the application itself
#   public/   served at the site's root
#   scripts/  small (204 KB) and referenced by npm scripts a future build step may call
#   drizzle/  migrations, read by the studio at runtime
